@startuml cmp_system_interfaces
title System interfaces - logical view (TCU as one black box, I-01 .. I-12)

left to right direction

actor "Console user" as User
package "Host tools (Pi5)" {
  component "Plant model" as Plant
  component "UDS tester" as Tester
  component "Console" as Console
}

rectangle "CAN path: can0 / slcand (I-10), SLCAN over USB VCOM (I-09), gateway FRDM-MCXN236, CAN bus (I-08)\n<<transparent>> every frame forwarded unchanged, no knowledge of xAT messages or UDS (DC-05, SIM-GW-001)" as Path {
  interface "I-01 SIM_Driver 0x100\nSelector, Brake, Throttle, AliveCtr\n10 ms, RX timeout 30 ms" as I01
  interface "I-02 SIM_Speed 0x101\nInputShaftSpeed, OutputShaftSpeed, AliveCtr\n10 ms, RX timeout 30 ms" as I02
  interface "I-03 SIM_Analog 0x102\nOilTempVoltage, LinePressVoltage, AliveCtr\n10 ms, RX timeout 30 ms" as I03
  interface "I-04 TCU_Actuators 0x200\nSS_A, SS_B, RLS, SLS, FaultLamp, PCS_Duty, AliveCtr\n10 ms (plant timeout 50 ms, SIM-PLT-004)" as I04
  interface "I-05 TCU_Status 0x201\nGearActual, GearTarget, Mode, SelectorState, ShiftInProgress,\nVehicleSpeed, FaultBits, OilTemp, AliveCtr; 100 ms" as I05
  interface "I-06 DIAG_PhysReq 0x7E1, DIAG_FuncReq 0x7DF\nUDS over ISO-TP; 0x7DF single frame, only 3E 80" as I06
  interface "I-07 DIAG_Resp 0x7E9\nUDS over ISO-TP; padding 0xCC, BS 0, STmin 0 ms" as I07
}

interface "I-11 debug status line, every 500 ms\nselector, gear, vehicle speed, mode, fault bits\n(debug UART, MCU-Link VCOM)" as I11
interface "I-12 red LED on the TCU board\nsame value as FaultLamp" as I12

component "TCU\nFRDM-MCXN947\n(black box:\napplication, PBL, SBL)" as TCU

User --> Console : I-14 keyboard / terminal
Console --> Plant : I-15 driver inputs, injected faults

Plant --> I01
Plant --> I02
Plant --> I03
I01 --> TCU
I02 --> TCU
I03 --> TCU

Plant <-- I04
Plant <-- I05
I04 <-- TCU
I05 <-- TCU

Tester --> I06
I06 --> TCU
Tester <-- I07
I07 <-- TCU

Console <.. I04 : display (SIM-CON-001)
Console <.. I05 : display (SIM-CON-001)
Console <-- I11 : read in a Pi5 terminal
I11 <-- TCU
User <-- I12 : light
I12 <-- TCU

note bottom of TCU
Covers: SYS-COM-001, SYS-COM-004, SYS-DIA-001, SYS-HMI-001, SYS-HMI-002,
SIM-GW-001, SIM-CON-001, SIM-CON-002, SIM-TST-004
Content and timing of I-01 .. I-07: can_matrix sections 2, 3, 5.
end note
@enduml
